meta {
  name: 27 EMI - Submit Result
  type: http
  seq: 27
}

get {
  url: {{emiBaseUrl}}/emi/submitResult
  body: text
  auth: none
}

headers {
  TOKEN: {{flowAdapterToken}}
  Content-Type: text/plain
}

body:text {
  {
    "specimen_type": "",
    "tube_information_id": "e9b6927a-f2e0-4898-910b-d892b45d8de1",
    "equipment_id": "11111112",
    "tube_no": "{{orderCode}}",
    "original_tube_no": "{{orderCode}}",
    "result_date": "1668583670356",
    "sent": "",
    "sent_date": "",
    "status": "-1",
    "local_db_status": "1",
    "test_results": [
      {
        "test_result_id": "b0a69d67-4434-44f0-b1e5-cf43f83bc536",
        "test_result": "{{emiResultValue}}",
        "test_name": "Hemoglobin",
        "display_name": "Hemoglobin",
        "universal_test_id": "{{emiParamCode}}",
        "unit": "{{emiParamUnit}}",
        "result_type": "",
        "specimen_types": []
      }
    ],
    "comment": "auto from analyzer (EMI E2E)",
    "token_id": "{{flowAdapterToken}}",
    "adapter_id": "14",
    "adapter_code": "erba-h560"
  }
}

script:post-response {
  const b = res.body;
  if (b && b.report_log && b.report_log.log && b.report_log.log.length) {
    bru.setVar("emiReportId", b.report_log.log[0].report_id);
  }
}

tests {
  test("result accepted (legacy s=200)", function () {
    expect(res.body.s).to.equal("200");
  });
  test("a report was filled", function () {
    expect(res.body.m).to.equal("Result updated successfully");
    expect(res.body.test_status).to.match(/test updated/);
    expect(res.body.report_log.log[0].fill_status).to.equal("Report filled");
  });
}

docs {
  **Machine step 2 — submit the result.** Exactly what a real analyzer sends:
  a **GET** to `/emi/submitResult` with a **JSON body under
  `Content-Type: text/plain`** (a legacy quirk — the server reads the raw body).
  Auth is the **`TOKEN`** header (`flowAdapterToken`).

  Key fields, all auto-filled from earlier steps:
  - `tube_no` = **`orderCode`** (the scanned id).
  - `test_results[0].universal_test_id` = **`emiParamCode`** (`HGB`) — matches the
    result parameter created on the lab test in step 14, so the value fills that
    parameter. `test_result` = `emiResultValue`, `unit` = `emiParamUnit`.

  The report is fillable (PENDING, from the accept in step 23) and its test is
  adapter-mapped, so the value is written with **`source = ADAPTER`** and the
  report moves to **`SAVED`**. Success →
  `{ "s": "200", "m": "Result updated successfully", "emi_status": "Complete",
  "test_status": "1 test updated", "report_log": { … log: [{ fill_status:
  "Report filled", … }] }, "prefered_test": { … }, "unique_test_ids": {} }`.
  Captures **`emiReportId`** from the report log.
}
